# Every text file is LF in the repository and on disk, whatever the operator's core.autocrlf says.
# Left to autocrlf, git checks out CRLF while scripts, formatters and Linux CI each write their own
# ending. A rewrite that changes only line endings then shows as a modified file with an empty diff.
# bash also rejects a CR on a shebang line, and yamllint reports CRLF as an error.
# Binary files are left alone: text=auto only converts what git detects as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe requires CRLF in batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
